  "body": "### What happened\n\nI was working in Setup2.   I did not have a machine selected for Setup1.   I selected a machine for Setup2 and it defaulted into Setup1.   \n\n<img width=\"310\" height=\"715\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/dc61bd80-be82-416b-a0e6-af68557c8430\" />\n\nSetups need to be able to have their own machine setup.   I think it is dangerous to default a machine selected in one setup into another setup.\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nSetup Setup1.   Leave the machine unselected. \nSetup Setup2.   Select a machine for it.    The same machine will be set in Setup1.\n\n\n### camcraft version and OS\n\nCamCraft 0.19.0 (release build) Build time: 2026-11-13 16:01 UTC Source commit: a2b357b48c6af61952c92a379ec426757d8a5cd8-dirty Platform: linux x86_64 GPU: gpu: adapter \"NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1070\" via vulkan Project: /home/me/Documents/Version 19 test.camproj Units: Millimeters Machine: Camcraft Tormach 1100MX (Mill, from built-in: Tormach 1100MX) Document: 2 setup(s), 1 model(s), 5 tool(s), 2 operation(s) (2 ok, 0 stale, 0 never generated) Status: generated Face2: 120 moves (1 plunge(s) @ 300, 1 level(s), 0 arc(s)), 0 warning(s)\n\n### Screenshots or recording\n\n_No response_",
